  <li><a href="#outcome">Outcome</a></li>
</ul>
<h3><a name="timeline" id="timeline">Time Line</a></h3>
            <table class="vote" summary="">
                <tr>
                  <th>Nomination period:</th>
                  <td>February 7<sup>th</sup> 00:00:01 UTC, 2004</td>
                  <td>February 28<sup>th</sup> 00:00:00 UTC, 2004</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Campaigning period:</th>
                  <td>February 28<sup>th</sup> 00:00:01 UTC, 2004</td>
                  <td>March 20<sup>th</sup> 00:00:00 UTC, 2004</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Voting period:</th>
                  <td>March 20<sup>th</sup>, 00:00:01 UTC, 2004</td>
                  <td>April 11<sup>th</sup>, 00:00:00 UTC, 2004</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p>Please note that the new term for the project leader shall start
               on April 17<sup>th</sup>, 2004.</p>
<h3><a name="nominations" id="nominations">Nominations</a></h3>
	    <ol>
	      <li>Martin Michlmayr [<a href="mailto:tbm@debian.org">tbm@debian.org</a>]
		      [<a href="platforms/tbm">platform</a>]</li>
	      <li>Gergely Nagy [<a href="mailto:algernon@debian.org">algernon@debian.org</a>]
		      [<a href="platforms/algernon">platform</a>]</li>
	      <li>Branden Robinson [<a href="mailto:branden@debian.org">branden@debian.org</a>]
		      [<a href="platforms/branden">platform</a>]</li>
	    </ol>
             <p>The ballot can be received through email by emailing
                <a href="mailto:ballot@vote.debian.org">ballot@vote.debian.org</a>
                with the subject leader2004. </p>
<h3><a name="statistics" id="statistics">Data and Statistics</a></h3>
          <p>
           Some
         <a href="leader2004_stats">statistics</a>
	  are being gathered about ballots and acknowledgements
	  periodically during the voting period. Additionally, the
   	  list of
           <a href="leader2004_voters.txt">people</a>
   	  who have voted is available. The
           <a href="leader2004_tally.txt">tally
             sheet</a> is also present.
         </p>
<h3><a name="quorum" id="quorum">Quorum</a></h3>
          <p>
	With <a href="vote_001.quorum.log">911 developers</a>,
	we have:
            <pre>
 Current Developer Count = 911
 Q ( sqrt(#devel) / 2 ) = 15.0913882727866
 K min(5, Q )           = 5
 Quorum  (3 x Q )       = 45.2741648183597


Option 1 Reached quorum: 144> 45.2741648183597
Option 2 Reached quorum: 394> 45.2741648183597
Option 3 Reached quorum: 442> 45.2741648183597

            </pre>
<h3><a name="majorityreq" id="majorityreq">Majority Requirement</a></h3>
	  <p>All three of these proposals require a simple majority.
             <pre>
Dropping Option 1 because of Majority.  0.558 (144/258) <= 1
Option 2 passes Majority.               5.629 (394/70)> 1
Option 3 passes Majority.              17.000 (442/26)> 1
	    </pre>
<h3><a name="outcome" id="outcome">Outcome</a></h3>
     	      <h3>The winner of the election is Martin Michlmayr</h3>
           <p>
    	     I would like to thank Branden Robinson and
              Gergely Nagy for their service to the project, for
              standing for the post of project leader, and for
              offering the developers a strong and viable group of
              candidates.
           </p>
           <p class="center">
             <a style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" href="vote_001_results.dot">
               <img src="vote_001_results.png" alt="Graphical rendering of the results" width="266" height="418">
               </a>
           </p>
           <p>
               Total unique votes cast: 482, which is 52.908891% of all
               possible votes.
           </p>
           <p>
               In the following table, tally[row x][col y] represents
               the votes that option x received over option y.
           </p>
           <ul>
             <li>Option 1 "Gergely Nagy"</li>
             <li>Option 2 "Branden Robinson"</li>
             <li>Option 3 "Martin Michlmayr"</li>
             <li>Option 4 "None of the Above"</li>
           </ul>
   	       <table class="vote" summary="">
                  <tr>
                    <th colspan="5" style="text-align:center;">Option</th>
	         </tr>
   	         <tr>
   	           <th>&nbsp;</th>
